      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can provide a general outline for the manifest and migration plan, but please note that a comprehensive solution would require detailed analysis of your specific infrastructure and requirements. \n\nHere's a general manifest of the current indexing structures:\n\n**Current Indexing Structure:**\n\n* Core archival indices:\n\t+ Primary keys (e.g., record IDs, ISBNs)\n\t+ Secondary keys (e.g., creation dates, author IDs)\n\t+ Full-text indexes (e.g., keyword search indexes)\n* Semantic metadata:\n\t+ Metadata standard (e.g., Dublin Core, MODS)\n\t+ Custom metadata (e.g., descriptive fields, bibliographic information)\n\nAnd here's a general plan for migrating the data:\n\n**Migration Plan:**\n\n1. Data mapping: Create a data mapping matrix to identify the relationships between your current indices and the new cloud-based cluster's data model.\n2. Index schema transfer: Transfer the indexing schema from the old cluster to the new cloud-based cluster.\n3. Record migration: Migrate the digitized records to the new cloud-based cluster, preserving the relational links between records.\n4. Metadata migration: Transfer the semantic metadata to the new cloud-based cluster, ensuring that the metadata standard and custom metadata are preserved and integrated correctly.\n5",
      "source": "target",
